{
  "sn12.67:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.67 ",
  "sn12.67:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.67:0.3": "Sheaves of Reeds ",
  "sn12.67:1.1": "At one time Venerable Sāriputta and Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita were staying near Varanasi in the deer park at Isipatana. ",
  "sn12.67:1.2": "Then in the late afternoon, Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita came out of retreat, went to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn12.67:1.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "sn12.67:1.4": "“Well, Reverend Sāriputta, are old age and death made by oneself? Or by another? Or by both oneself and another? Or do they arise anomalously, not made by oneself or another?” ",
  "sn12.67:1.5": "“No, Reverend Koṭṭhita, old age and death are not made by oneself, nor by another, nor by both oneself and another, nor do they arise anomalously, not made by oneself or another. ",
  "sn12.67:1.6": "Rather, rebirth is a requirement for old age and death.” ",
  "sn12.67:2.1": "“Well, Reverend Sāriputta, is rebirth made by oneself? Or by another? Or by both oneself and another? Or does it arise anomalously, not made by oneself or another?” ",
  "sn12.67:2.2": "“No, Reverend Koṭṭhita, rebirth is not made by oneself, nor by another, nor by both oneself and another, nor does it arise anomalously, not made by oneself or another. ",
  "sn12.67:2.3": "Rather, continued existence is a requirement for rebirth.” ",
  "sn12.67:3.1": "“Wel